// issues/fixed/derive-clone-over-an-arraylist-field-emits-a-hollow-clone.md
// The CONTAINER-field variant of the non-clone-field derive. `ArrayList` is
// a `Deref` type (VERDICTS-63), so the generated body clones the field
// through its own impl, `(type_of(self.rel) <: Clone).clone(&self.rel)`,
// and the cast fails: `ArrayList(R)` is `Clone` only when `R` is. Expected:
// an error at the derive line naming `ArrayList(R)` and `Clone`; before the
// `Deref` impl it was E0610 inside std's Clone impl, naming `R`
// (check-derive-clone-non-clone-field is the direct variant).
{ ArrayList } :: import("std/collections/array-list");
{ println } :: import("std/fmt");
R :: struct(a : usize);
S :: struct(x : usize, rel : ArrayList(R));
derive(S, Clone);
main :: (fn() -> unit)({
  s := S(x : usize(2), rel : ArrayList(R).new());
  c := s.clone();
  println((s.x + c.x).to_string());
  ()
});
export(main);
